         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### In Multiplication, the Order Does Not Matter\n\nRemember: **multiplication is a repeated addition**. When we multiply, we add the same number many times.\n\n**2 × 5 = 10** means: **5 + 5 = 10** — the five, added two times.\n**5 × 2 = 10** means: **2 + 2 + 2 + 2 + 2 = 10** — the two, added five times.\n\nIn both cases, we add the same squares, so the result is always 10! It is like counting with our hands: we can count **two hands with five fingers** (2 × 5 = 10) or **five pairs of fingers** (5 × 2 = 10) — joining thumb with thumb, index with index, and so on, we make five pairs of two fingers.\n\nIn any order, we always reach our ten fingers. The order of the numbers does not change the result!",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
