         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Conclusion\n\nFantastic! In this class, we learned that multiplication is a **repeated addition** and that the **order of the numbers does not change the result**.\n\nThere are **four ways** to group ten:\n**1 × 10 = 10** (one line with ten squares)\n**2 × 5 = 10** (two lines with five squares)\n**5 × 2 = 10** (five lines with two squares)\n**10 × 1 = 10** (ten lines with one square)\n\nWhichever way we choose, we always count ten! Now you know a secret of multiplication: the order does not change the result.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
